// Audit note (2026-11-03) -- why these three keep a bare `new V{...}`:
// V2dDrawTrSurfDrawable / V2dPolyPolygon2d / V2dPolyPolygon3d are built from a
// freshly allocated object at every call site (`new Draw_Marker2D(...)`,
// `new Poly_Polygon2D(n)`, `new DrawTrSurf_Point(...)`, ...). A fresh
// allocation cannot be a null handle; if it throws, the enclosing catch already
// returns nullptr. So occt2d_wrap_handle<V>() would guard a case that cannot
// happen -- it would only hide the invariant. Do NOT mechanically convert these
// 20 sites; the generated handle *getters* (which can return a null handle from
// OCCT) are the ones that need the wrapper.
